.TitleBlockAnnotation
Attributes orient=N0 x=3720 y=2880  
TextBlockInfo company="Texas Instruments" title="TPS62903, 3-V to 17-V, High Efficiency and Low IQ Buck Converter in 1.5-mm × 2-mm QFN Package" author="Texas Instruments" notes="1.   The TPS62903 model is encrypted and will run in versions 8.40i and above.\n2.   The testbench has been configured VIN = 12V, VOUT = 1.2V and Iload = 3A.\n3.   The model has been corner tested for an input voltage range of 3V to 17V and a load current range of 100mA to 3A.\n4.   To run the POP/AC analysis, you must run complete Startup Transient simulation and then run the AC analysis.\n      Also you must choose \"Use snapshot from previous transient analysis\" in POP Advanced options.\n5.   All transients can be applied after the output voltage reaches steady-state. \n6.   The operating quiescent current and shutdown current have not been modeled.\n7.   Thermal shutdown characteristics of the part have not been modeled.\n8.   The simulation runs for 2.1ms and takes approximately 17 seconds to run on a quad core 2.8GHz machine.\n      Then AC simulation runs from 1kHz to 1MHz and takes 13 seconds to run on a quad core 2.8GHz machine." layout="Horizontal" image="" version="" 
Property name="StyleNormal" value="DefaultTitleBlock" autopos=1 normal=Left rotated=Left visible=0 font=Default order=-1
Property name="StyleSelected" value="DefaultTitleBlockSelected" autopos=1 normal=Left rotated=Left visible=0 font=Default order=-1
.EndTitleBlockAnnotation
Text value=".simulator SIMPLIS\n*.ac DEC 25 1k 1Meg\n.options\n+ PSP_START=0\n+ PSP_NPT=10001\n+ POP_ITRMAX=20\n+ POP_USE_TRAN_SNAPSHOT\n+ POP_OUTPUT_CYCLES=5\n+ SNAPSHOT_INTVL=0\n+ MIN_AVG_TOPOLOGY_DUR=1a\n+ AVG_TOPOLOGY_DUR_MEASUREMENT_WINDOW=128\n*.pop TRIG_GATE={TRIG_GATE} TRIG_COND=0_TO_1 MAX_PERIOD=1u CONVERGENCE=1p CYCLES_BEFORE_LAUNCH=5 TD_RUN_AFTER_POP_FAILS=-1\n.tran 2.01m 2m\n\n.simulator DEFAULT\n\n*$\n* TPS62903\n*****************************************************************************\n* (C) Copyright 2021 Texas Instruments Incorporated. All rights reserved.                                            \n*****************************************************************************\n** This model is designed as an aid for customers of Texas Instruments.\n** TI and its licensors and suppliers make no warranties, either expressed\n** or implied, with respect to this model, including the warranties of \n** merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose.  The model is\n** provided solely on an \"as is\" basis.  The entire risk as to its quality\n** and performance is with the customer\n*****************************************************************************\n*\n* This model is subject to change without notice. Texas Instruments\n* Incorporated is not responsible for updating this model.\n*\n*****************************************************************************\n*\n** Released by: Texas Instruments Inc.\n* Part: TPS62903\n* Date: 27SEP2021\n* Model Type: TRANSIENT, AVERAGE\n* Simulator: SIMPLIS\n* Simulator Version: 8.40i\n* EVM Order Number: TPS62903EVM-069\n* EVM Users Guide: SNVU745A – JANUARY 2021 – REVISED MAY 2021\n* Datasheet: SLVSES3A – FEBRUARY 2021 – REVISED MARCH 2021 \n* Topologies Supported: Buck, Inverting Buck Boost\n*\n* Model Version: Final 1.00\n*\n*****************************************************************************\n*\n* Updates:\n*\n* Final 1.00\n* Release to Web.\n*\n*****************************************************************************\n*\n* Model Usage Notes:\n* A. Features have been modelled\n*\t1. \tOutput Voltage Setting\n*\t2. \tInternal Fixed Soft-Start and External Adjustable Soft-start\n*\t3. \tFrequency and Operation Mode Selection\n*\t4. \tHigh-side FET Current Limit\n*\t5.  Low-side FET Current Limit\n*\t6.\tLow-side FET Sink Current Limit\n*\t7. \tPower Good\n*\t8.  Output Voltage Discharge\n*\t9.  UVLO Protection\n*\n* B. Features have not been modelled\n*\t1. Operating Quiescent Current\n*   2. Shutdown Current \n*   3. Temperature dependent characteristics\n*\n* C. Application Notes \n*   1. To run the POP/AC analysis, you must run complete Startup Transient simulation and then run the AC analysis.\n*\t   Also you must choose \"Use snapshot from previous transient analysis\" in POP Advanced options.\n*\n*****************************************************************************\n.subckt TPS62903_TRANS  139 133 113 135 101 144 103 127 128\n\n.node_map SS_TR 139\n.node_map FB_VSET 133\n.node_map MODE_SCONF 113\n.node_map PG 135\n.node_map EN 101\n.node_map VOS 144\n.node_map VIN 103\n.node_map VSW 127\n.node_map GND 128\n\n*\n?@@--START ENCRYPTION: \"SMX_AES TPS62903 TRANS\"\n?@@j/lbrFOqUMy6NW/GDHVDUW6m4qhN2Njnw+BDnY9r4/EbzUn+cIj1/LUsFnXKK0hp?##\n?@@dQ4mDPNles+7HBbDAniXbPRSQb9MDWPXN7HsoYQ2w4guEgVJhsdvWK33yuMCmx7w?##\n?@@k2X2SzOd9wCYHeLYvE+VkysDBV4y78obNzPadJYZwlrk05H9Km+vIjntQBPXIa1O?##\n?@@PXoKI9aLQw4OAS+fcrNCYeRRP/0UzaPjudPQjFB5U++rGQ/gldt7X5EuXU+dYFaY?##\n?@@Arkwcwh5BU8OVJ/Z6kLeblTGCLN48Fyd3ARiy0WiRYt8L1Pso44SoPeQX8k74Cub?##\n?@@BvRyy6MwRxtHYnuezesZr6IJxmrVRJl17r6KL/wfKrhDnCGVhUBLI+oUDxdFiatf?##\n?@@1MxCEFum7u93k1dO8bwjIA0mTkHdrQ5sI3egJa/sVRLac58TWVw7u5f5BsBiXwq3?##\n?@@1m6r/zNzhrc9OHmuVAdtXjOEk4uJIysL3VF9qA7Zp/6M0274DWek8vD7QFtLQPcw?##\n?@@NtrbFmbdUFr8B1dYFoxZ8Qze8GiaLnE9vdgzmHti5SXEVQ+YvvnV6v9RpWoaEm0R?##\n?@@K482Q5UuPszXCWg7AeSdtTm/oGgiRUQThDoUf1odbfuPErOzCn4GjwX7cKXGUKtb?##\n?@@JmDWGTEQ3OeXRem3R/mOToYnwOUN5lr22k13rUpWyItRMzwQmAe0WdUblnYMGwld